limactl-start.log
=================

The transcript internal/narrate is tested against. Its whole value is
provenance: patterns written from memory, tested against lines written from
the same memory, prove nothing about what lima actually prints.

THIS COPY IS CAPTURED.

    captured   2026-08-19
    lima       limactl version 2.2.0
    host       macOS, Apple Silicon
    command    limactl start --name=sandbox-test <rendered claude-repo.yaml>
    state      instance deleted first, so this is a create, not a re-start;
               ~/Library/Caches/lima/download removed first, so the image
               download lines are real rather than a cache hit

The only edit is $HOME replaced by /Users/you. Nothing else is touched: the
SSH local port, the digest, the timestamps and their spacing, the instance
name, the line ordering, and the four benign "address already in use"
warnings for port 5355 are all as lima emitted them. Each further edit would
weaken the only claim this file makes.

WHAT IT REPLACED, AND WHY THAT IS THE POINT

The previous copy was reconstructed from lima's message shapes while ptrbox
was built on Linux against a faked limactl. It used logrus's INFO[0049]
default text format, which lima did emit historically. Lima 2.2.0 emits
time="..." level=info msg="...", so zero of the 65 real lines matched
narrate.go's entry pattern, and the whole translator had been a no-op in
production while its suite stayed green. The fixture and the patterns were two
expressions of one wrong recollection, written in the same sitting. See TODO
24 in CLAUDE.md for the full inventory.

narrate.go was rewritten against THIS copy (TODO 24), and the tests now quote
it rather than paraphrase it: the elapsed times in narrate_test.go are
differences between timestamps below, "ok after 1m16s" is this file's optional
requirement, and the line counts are its counts. So a re-capture whose shape
differs fails the suite loudly instead of passing it silently, which is the
one thing the previous copy could not do.

The lima version above is load-bearing. A future release can change this
format again; when it does, the symptom is once more a silent degradation to
"everything shown dimmed and verbatim", because that is the designed failure
path. Green tests will not tell you. Re-capturing will.

RE-CAPTURING

    limactl delete -f sandbox-test
    rm -rf ~/Library/Caches/lima/download
    limactl start --name=sandbox-test ~/.lima/_generated/sandbox-test.yaml 2>&1 \
      | tee internal/narrate/testdata/limactl-start.log
    sed -i '' "s|$HOME|/Users/you|g" internal/narrate/testdata/limactl-start.log

Then run `make test` and read what changed. Add a pattern to narrate.go by
adding a line to this file first, never the other way round.

Not a .md file on purpose: this repo gitignores *.md, and a note about a
fixture's trustworthiness is worth less than nothing if it is untracked.

limafake replays this file when a test asks it to (internal/cli/voice_test.go
sets it as StartOutput), so the command-level tests and the translator's own
tests run on identical bytes.


limactl-start-reboot.log
========================

The second authority (TODO 27): the same command against an instance that
already exists, which is the path `ptrbox new`'s reboot and every
`ptrbox start` take - the common path, since a VM is created once and
resumed many times.

THIS COPY IS CAPTURED.

    captured   2026-08-28
    lima       the same install as the cold capture (2.2.0 on 2026-08-19);
               the format is byte-compatible with it. If lima has been
               upgraded and this line not corrected, re-read the version.
    host       macOS, Apple Silicon
    command    limactl stop scratch; limactl start scratch
    state      instance existed and was provisioned; image cache warm and
               irrelevant - a reboot never consults it, which is why this
               file has no image lines at all

Same editing rule: $HOME replaced by /Users/you, nothing else touched.

What it justified: exactly one new pattern, `Using the existing instance` -
every other line already appears, shape for shape, in the cold capture.
TODO 27 predicted three shapes; the other two are NOT here and therefore
still have no patterns:

  - "Using cache" belongs to a warm-cache CREATE (lima logs "Attempting to
    download the image" and then does not download). A reboot never reaches
    that code. Capturing one means `limactl delete` + `ptrbox new` with the
    cache intact, teeing the start.
  - the waitless satisfied-requirement during shutdown belongs to `limactl
    stop` output, which has never been captured. Its symptom is already
    handled defensively (an unattached "satisfied" names its phase), but
    the stop stream as a whole still renders verbatim.

Both files are replayed: the translator's tests read each directly, and
limafake serves the cold capture for a create (StartOutput) and this one for
a restart (RestartOutput), which is the same split real lima makes.
